# Architecture

Reference: `architecture/atomic-design.md`, `architecture/section-structure.md`, `architecture/component-naming.md`.

## Atomic Design

- **Atoms**: single-purpose UI primitives (Button, Heading, Input).
- **Molecules**: small combinations with one responsibility (Form Field, Text Block).
- **Organisms**: reusable composites (Navigation, Hero Content, FAQ Accordion).
- **Layouts**: `Section` (wrapper → container → slot) — separate from content components. Grids/columns live in content components.
- **Pages**: assemble sections; do not duplicate reusable logic.

## Composition rules

- Reuse existing components before creating new ones.
- Use variants for shared structure with different content.
- Avoid giant components with unrelated conditionals.
- Do not force simple UI into unnecessary abstraction layers.
- Do not classify every nested component as an organism.

## Separation of concerns

- Content vs presentation: keep copy/data out of presentational styling logic when possible.
- Data fetching vs UI: fetch/normalize upstream; render pure UI from typed props.
- Section vs content: sections own layout boundaries and spacing; content components own presentation.

## Naming

- Name by responsibility (`SplitContent`, `FeatureGrid`), not page placement.
- PascalCase component files; kebab-case CSS classes; camelCase JS/TS identifiers.
